---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('pulsewire')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 23, 2026';
const sections = [
  { href: '#availability', label: 'Availability and access' },
  { href: '#sessions', label: 'Sign-in and sessions' },
  { href: '#offline', label: 'Offline Saved copies' },
  { href: '#sources-ai', label: 'Sources and AI' },
  { href: '#data-controls', label: 'Export and deletion' },
  { href: '#troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { href: '#contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  app={app}
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with PulseWire private access, the read-only demo, Entra sessions, source freshness, AI processing, offline Saved snapshots, and current data-control gaps."
  path="/pulsewire/support"
  page="support"
  heading="PulseWire Support"
  documentMeta={`Updated ${updatedDate} · Web and installable PWA`}
  summary="PulseWire is a private web reader and installable PWA. The owner workspace uses Microsoft Entra; a separate 24-hour read-only demo creates no personal account. There is no native iOS or Android app."
  sections={sections}
  evidenceNote="Availability, session, offline, retention, and account-control guidance was checked against immutable PulseWire release-visual authority 6b4c1c7 on August 23, 2026."
>
  <section id="availability" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Current availability and access</h2>
    <p class="legal-callout">
      PulseWire has no public account registration. Owner access is restricted to
      configured Microsoft Entra principals. The service landing page also offers
      a read-only demo session that expires after 24 hours and does not save
      personal changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The web app can be installed as a PWA in a supported browser. Installing it
      does not make the full workspace local-first and does not create a separate
      device account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sessions" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Microsoft sign-in and session controls</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If owner sign-in is rejected, confirm the intended Microsoft account and
        ask support to verify that its Entra principal is authorized.
      </li>
      <li>
        Settings can revoke the current session or use
        <strong>Sign out all devices</strong> for owner sessions.
      </li>
      <li>
        Sign-out clears identity-scoped offline data before the server session is
        revoked. If that clear fails, PulseWire blocks sign-out and asks you to
        recover rather than silently leaving private data behind.
      </li>
      <li>
        Demo sessions cannot use the owner’s all-device revoke control and expire
        on their own.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Revoking PulseWire sessions does not sign out of, disable, or delete the
      underlying Microsoft account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="offline" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Offline Saved copies</h2>
    <p>
      Choose the offline action on a Saved story while connected. PulseWire
      downloads a sanitized text snapshot to IndexedDB in that browser profile;
      article images are not included. Offline access applies only to explicitly
      downloaded Saved items, not the whole edition, search, live sources, or AI.
    </p>
    <p>
      The local copy is not end-to-end encrypted. Remove it before sharing a
      browser profile or device. If a download appears stale, reconnect, open the
      Saved item, remove the local copy, and download it again after the current
      server snapshot loads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sources-ai" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Source freshness and generated briefs</h2>
    <p>
      A feed or article can be late or unavailable because the publisher changed
      its feed, blocked a request, removed a page, or returned an error. Retry
      later and compare the story with its linked source. Opening a source leaves
      PulseWire and loads the publisher’s site under that publisher’s terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Briefs, embeddings, and grouping use configured Azure AI Foundry
      deployments. Generated text can be incomplete or wrong, and an AI feature
      can pause when provider or service controls are unavailable. Treat source
      evidence as authoritative and report a repeatable mismatch with the story
      title and time observed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-controls" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Export, account deletion, and retention</h2>
    <p>
      PulseWire does not currently provide a self-service account export or
      account-deletion control. A downloaded Saved snapshot is an offline reading
      copy, not a full workspace export. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a> to
      start a manual access or deletion review.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting or revoking PulseWire data does not delete the Microsoft account,
      Microsoft sign-in records, publisher records, or provider-held operational
      data. The <a href="/pulsewire/privacy">PulseWire Privacy Policy</a> lists the
      current article-retention tiers and Saved-snapshot exceptions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting checklist</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Reconnect and reload the current page once.</li>
      <li>Confirm the correct owner or demo session is active.</li>
      <li>For owner access, check whether another device can open the workspace.</li>
      <li>
        For an offline issue, remain online until the Saved snapshot finishes
        downloading, then test that specific item offline.
      </li>
      <li>
        If the problem repeats, record the browser, operating system, time,
        affected story or feature, and the visible recovery message.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not send Microsoft passwords, verification codes, cookies, access tokens,
      private source credentials, or a complete private workspace export.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Contact and legal documents</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> for product
      support. Include only the minimum story title or screenshot needed to
      explain the problem. For data handling, read the
      <a href="/pulsewire/privacy">PulseWire Privacy Policy</a>. Use of PulseWire
      is subject to the <a href="/terms">Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
